      "original_decoder_run_sha256": "b60815491e3b8112b37bc386c5ed5358c9c9a81d51f72a5b5987a6d2f295c688",
      "reconstructed_theorem_text": "Let E and S be types. E has a normed additive commutative group structure, a real inner product space structure, is complete and finite dimensional over the reals, and has a measurable space structure equal to its Borel structure; S has an arbitrary measurable space structure. Let V:E→R and κ∈R. Assume κ≥1, V is twice continuously Frechet differentiable over R, and for every x,v∈E the real Hessian quadratic form satisfies κ^{-1}||v||^2 ≤ D(DV)(x)[v][v] ≤ ||v||^2. Let eta:S→R and y:S→E be measurable, and assume eta(s)>0 for every s∈S. Define F(s,x)=V(x)+(eta(s)^{-1}/2)||x-y(s)||^2 for all s∈S and x∈E.\nThere exists one function p:S→E such that p is measurable and all the following hold simultaneously. For every s∈S, p(s)+eta(s)∇V(p(s))=y(s). For every s∈S and z∈E, F(s,p(s))+((κ^{-1}+eta(s)^{-1})/2)||z-p(s)||^2 ≤ F(s,z), and F(s,z)≤F(s,p(s)) if and only if z=p(s). For every s,t∈S, if eta(s)=eta(t), then ||p(s)-p(t)||≤||y(s)-y(t)||. Define G:S×E→E by G(s,z)=∇V(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s)) z), with multiplication of a real and a vector interpreted as scalar multiplication. This G is measurable on the product measurable space. For every s,t∈S and z,w∈E, if eta(s)=eta(t), then ||G(s,z)-G(t,w)||≤||y(s)-y(t)||+sqrt(eta(s))||z-w||. There exists a measurable measure-valued kernel K from S to E such that every K(s) is a probability measure and, for every s∈S, K(s) is exactly the pushforward of the canonical centered covariance-identity Gaussian measure on E under z↦G(s,z).\nAll points, directions and noise variables range over the full carrier E. The gradient is the Riesz representative of the actual Frechet derivative. The same p determines F's minimizers, G, and K. Equal eta values are hypotheses only of the two pairwise Lipschitz statements. No restriction eta≤1 occurs. E may have dimension zero, and S need not have topology, a measure, or be nonempty. K is the Gaussian gradient-output law specified above; no posterior conditional Gibbs law or HMC transition is asserted.",
